00:09:23.491 --> 00:09:26.954
(electronic music)

00:09:26.954 --> 00:09:28.940
Tip number five is have a business model.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:32.023
You got to figure out how to
make money off of this, right?

00:09:32.023 --> 00:09:33.922
You're posting all this
content to social media.

00:09:33.922 --> 00:09:36.117
You have to have a
business model around it

00:09:36.117 --> 00:09:38.902
that feeds the system,
that feeds the content,

00:09:38.902 --> 00:09:40.470
that allows you to build a team.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:43.295
When I started, you know,
I hate making content,

00:09:43.295 --> 00:09:45.936
I hate investing anything with money

00:09:45.936 --> 00:09:47.210
until I'm making money, right?

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.246
I hate spending money
until I'm making money.

00:09:48.246 --> 00:09:49.079
So I got to figure out a way.

00:09:49.079 --> 00:09:51.527
How do I make money off of
everything that I'm doing?

00:09:51.527 --> 00:09:53.636
Or the project is just a hobby?

00:09:53.636 --> 00:09:55.874
Or the project dies
because I can't figure out

00:09:55.874 --> 00:09:57.194
a business model around it.

00:09:57.194 --> 00:09:59.444
So with some networks, it's easier.

00:09:59.444 --> 00:10:01.374
With YouTube, they have
built-in advertising,

00:10:01.374 --> 00:10:02.560
so you can do that.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.024
There's brand deals that are available.

00:10:04.024 --> 00:10:05.952
You can sell your own merch
and different products.

00:10:05.952 --> 00:10:07.507
There's a page around now that exists

00:10:07.507 --> 00:10:09.455
that you can have your fans help find you.

00:10:09.455 --> 00:10:11.794
A little bit harder with
the other platforms.

00:10:11.794 --> 00:10:14.906
They haven't figured out the
monetization as much yet.

00:10:14.906 --> 00:10:16.272
It could be for your business.

00:10:16.272 --> 00:10:18.128
Toronto Dance Salsa has a business.

00:10:18.128 --> 00:10:19.573
It's on social media.

00:10:19.573 --> 00:10:21.570
We don't care about making
money from the videos

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:23.318
or from Twitter or brand deals.

00:10:23.318 --> 00:10:25.862
It's about getting people
to sign up for salsa classes

00:10:25.862 --> 00:10:27.037
and take lessons with us.

00:10:27.037 --> 00:10:28.131
That's the main driver.

00:10:28.131 --> 00:10:30.850
So whether you're
selling a product service

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:32.080
on the outside world,

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:34.803
whether you're trying to sell
to a specific demographic,

00:10:34.803 --> 00:10:36.668
whether you're doing
advertising or brand deals,

00:10:36.668 --> 00:10:39.361
understanding what your business model is

00:10:39.361 --> 00:10:41.997
and then driving towards that
to try to make some money

00:10:41.997 --> 00:10:45.097
so you can not just support
yourself, but build a team.

00:10:45.097 --> 00:10:46.039
There's so many YouTubers.

00:10:46.039 --> 00:10:47.332
I went to Clamour Con.

00:10:47.332 --> 00:10:48.685
There's so many YouTubers with channels

00:10:48.685 --> 00:10:51.048
that are bigger than mine,

00:10:51.048 --> 00:10:53.123
that they're still doing
everything themselves

00:10:53.123 --> 00:10:56.560
and they can't afford to
have anybody on their team.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.211
They don't have a
business model around it.

00:10:58.211 --> 00:11:00.901
They're just trying to drive
views and make content,

00:11:00.901 --> 00:11:02.604
which is great and they love it.

00:11:02.604 --> 00:11:04.016
But it's still just a hobby for them.

00:11:04.016 --> 00:11:05.966
They need a business model around it,

00:11:05.966 --> 00:11:08.809
and it was shocking that people
with millions of subscribers

00:11:08.809 --> 00:11:11.162
still aren't making a
full-time income from it

00:11:11.162 --> 00:11:13.910
and can't afford to hire
somebody underneath them.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:15.600
Depends on the niche,
depends on a few factors,

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:17.924
but you got to be able to build
a business model around it

00:11:17.924 --> 00:11:20.502
so you can support
yourself and set to build

00:11:20.502 --> 00:11:22.556
a team to make your content more valuable.

00:11:22.556 --> 00:11:25.733
(electronic music)

00:11:25.733 --> 00:11:28.391
Which leads into number six,
which is to build a team!

00:11:28.391 --> 00:11:29.491
You know, if you want to make

00:11:29.491 --> 00:11:32.413
consistent, great
quality, awesome content,

00:11:32.413 --> 00:11:33.911
you need to build a team.

00:11:33.911 --> 00:11:35.853
You have to recognize
what you are fantastic at,

00:11:35.853 --> 00:11:38.420
what are you best in
the world at, and then,

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.853
or potentially best in the
world if you're not there yet,

00:11:40.853 --> 00:11:43.503
and then surround yourself with
people who can do the rest.

00:11:43.503 --> 00:11:45.945
So for me, editing is
not what I'm great at.

00:11:45.945 --> 00:11:49.219
For me, being a videographer
is not what I'm great at.

00:11:49.219 --> 00:11:51.169
If you go back to my videos,
you'll see that they look worse

00:11:51.169 --> 00:11:52.568
than what they do right now.

00:11:52.568 --> 00:11:54.400
The camera's worse, the
editing is way worse.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.079
I'm way worse on camera as well.

00:11:57.079 --> 00:11:59.564
But I chose to spend my time

00:11:59.564 --> 00:12:01.288
focusing on being a better speaker

00:12:01.288 --> 00:12:04.655
and being better on the
research to pick the clips

00:12:04.655 --> 00:12:07.261
that are going to make it into
the final versions for you guys,

00:12:07.261 --> 00:12:09.350
and everything else gets assigned
to the people on my team.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:11.928
So there's eight people
who work on my YouTube team

00:12:11.928 --> 00:12:13.242
with different functions.

00:12:13.242 --> 00:12:15.916
Some a full-time basis,
some in a part-time basis.

00:12:15.916 --> 00:12:17.813
And that will allow us
to make more content.

00:12:17.813 --> 00:12:19.091
How do you move from one video a week

00:12:19.091 --> 00:12:21.123
to two a day to three a day?

00:12:21.123 --> 00:12:23.143
How do you keep the consistency up

00:12:23.143 --> 00:12:24.640
and the quality level up?

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:25.615
It's with a team.

00:12:25.615 --> 00:12:27.549
And so that's where you
get more subscribers.

00:12:27.549 --> 00:12:31.589
And it can start with
just one project, right?

00:12:31.589 --> 00:12:35.063
The very first person that
I hired for my business,

00:12:35.063 --> 00:12:36.701
we just made one
collaboration video together.

00:12:36.701 --> 00:12:37.744
And that did well.

00:12:37.744 --> 00:12:39.260
So, I went, okay, that did well

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.741
so we can work on something else.

00:12:40.741 --> 00:12:42.079
As soon as I made money on my channel,

00:12:42.079 --> 00:12:43.716
I poured it back into the business

00:12:43.716 --> 00:12:45.777
to bring on my team so I can build it up,

00:12:45.777 --> 00:12:48.186
build it up, build it up, build it up.

00:12:48.186 --> 00:12:49.849
And so, you want to start eyeing,

00:12:49.849 --> 00:12:52.165
what is the thing you hate
doing most in your business,

00:12:52.165 --> 00:12:54.504
in your YouTube channel,
or in your social media?

00:12:54.504 --> 00:12:56.135
If it's the graphic
design, it's the editing,

00:12:56.135 --> 00:12:57.207
it's the filming, the research,

00:12:57.207 --> 00:12:58.513
whatever it is that you hate the most.

00:12:58.513 --> 00:13:00.194
Some people love being behind the camera.

00:13:00.194 --> 00:13:01.552
They don't want to be in front.

00:13:01.552 --> 00:13:02.893
Great, go partner up.

00:13:02.893 --> 00:13:04.347
It doesn't even have to be paid, right?

00:13:04.347 --> 00:13:06.521
There's some people, if you love editing,

00:13:06.521 --> 00:13:08.910
there's people who love
being in front of the camera

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.936
and are looking for experience
in front of the camera.

00:13:10.936 --> 00:13:12.001
Go work with them.

00:13:12.001 --> 00:13:13.585
You don't have to pay them at the start.

00:13:13.585 --> 00:13:14.854
Just build up your portfolio,

00:13:14.854 --> 00:13:16.638
get your experience, get better.

00:13:16.638 --> 00:13:19.141
Build up content, start
making a little bit of money,

00:13:19.141 --> 00:13:20.011
and then you can afford

00:13:20.011 --> 00:13:22.211
to have a budget to go and hire people.

00:13:22.211 --> 00:13:25.153
(electronic music)

00:13:25.153 --> 00:13:27.281
And tip number seven is model success.

00:13:27.281 --> 00:13:28.284
And I love this tip.

00:13:28.284 --> 00:13:29.911
It's always one of my go-to's.

00:13:29.911 --> 00:13:31.289
If you're trying to figure out

00:13:31.289 --> 00:13:33.149
what you should be doing in a new market,

00:13:33.149 --> 00:13:34.693
one of the fastest ways of doing it

00:13:34.693 --> 00:13:36.568
is look at what people are currently doing

00:13:36.568 --> 00:13:37.401
and learn from them.

00:13:37.401 --> 00:13:38.486
It doesn't mean you copy them.

00:13:38.486 --> 00:13:39.882
You could learn a lot from my channel.

00:13:39.882 --> 00:13:41.652
If you try to just copy me,

00:13:41.652 --> 00:13:43.305
you're never going to
have massive success.

00:13:43.305 --> 00:13:44.546
You'll just be an Evan Junior.

00:13:44.546 --> 00:13:47.060
But you could learn from some
of the things that I'm doing

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.450
and apply it to your channel.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:51.686
You could also learn from other industries

00:13:51.686 --> 00:13:53.292
and bring them to your business.

00:13:53.292 --> 00:13:56.583
So, you all, I learned
a lot for my channel

00:13:56.583 --> 00:13:58.055
from guys like Darrel Eves,

00:13:58.055 --> 00:13:59.035
from guys like Tim Schmoyer,

00:13:59.035 --> 00:14:00.343
from guys like Casey Neistat,

00:14:00.343 --> 00:14:01.703
from guys like Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:14:01.703 --> 00:14:04.261
I learned from these people
who have done a lot more

00:14:04.261 --> 00:14:06.130
and in a lot of cases,
my channel now has grown

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.642
to be bigger than their channels.

00:14:07.642 --> 00:14:09.956
I've learned from them, and I
keep learning from more people

00:14:09.956 --> 00:14:11.482
to make myself better.

00:14:11.482 --> 00:14:14.329
I've learned from outside
industry, from the business world

00:14:14.329 --> 00:14:15.904
that say hey, I think it's important

00:14:15.904 --> 00:14:17.806
that everybody gets a
reply in their comments.

00:14:17.806 --> 00:14:20.480
So I'm going to hire a team
of people to help me do that,

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:23.578
where most YouTube creators
can't keep up with the comments

00:14:23.578 --> 00:14:25.093
so they just leave it.

00:14:25.093 --> 00:14:27.315
They respond for 20 minutes after a video,

00:14:27.315 --> 00:14:28.325
and then that's it.

00:14:28.325 --> 00:14:29.158
They're gone.

00:14:29.158 --> 00:14:30.597
I want everybody to get a response

00:14:30.597 --> 00:14:31.693
so I build up a team.

00:14:31.693 --> 00:14:32.853
And that just comes
from the business world.

00:14:32.853 --> 00:14:34.321
If you look at Logan Paul

00:14:34.321 --> 00:14:36.336
and the success that he's
had with his YouTube channel,

00:14:36.336 --> 00:14:38.713
one of the fastest growing
YouTube channels of all time,

00:14:38.713 --> 00:14:40.106
he came from the Vine world

00:14:40.106 --> 00:14:42.682
and had success really quickly on YouTube,

00:14:42.682 --> 00:14:46.070
implementing the strategies
that worked for him in Vine,

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:48.918
the six second videos,
applying them to YouTube.

00:14:48.918 --> 00:14:50.693
And really capturing people
of short attention spans

00:14:50.693 --> 00:14:52.737
and making high quality content

00:14:52.737 --> 00:14:54.473
around him and on his vlogs.

00:14:54.473 --> 00:14:57.677
So you can learn both from
people inside your industry

00:14:57.677 --> 00:14:59.442
who you look up to, who
have had a lot of success

00:14:59.442 --> 00:15:01.422
as well as people outside of the industry.

00:15:01.422 --> 00:15:03.136
You can say huh, if I bring this,

00:15:03.136 --> 00:15:04.914
this is something new that doesn't exist

00:15:04.914 --> 00:15:06.097
that hasn't been done before.

00:15:06.097 --> 00:15:08.395
I'm going to bring it and see if it works!

00:15:08.395 --> 00:15:09.228
Try it, test it.

00:15:09.228 --> 00:15:10.286
If it doesn't work, you can drop it.

00:15:10.286 --> 00:15:12.390
But if it does, you run with it.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:14.454
So that's my take on the
seven tips and tricks

00:15:14.454 --> 00:15:15.759
to quickly get more subscribers.

00:15:15.759 --> 00:15:18.558
I made this for you because
Luke Stinson asked me to.

00:15:18.558 --> 00:15:20.506
So if there is a topic
you want me to cover

00:15:20.506 --> 00:15:21.771
in a future seven ways,

00:15:21.771 --> 00:15:23.597
check out the link in the subscription.

00:15:23.597 --> 00:15:25.653
You can go and cast your vote.

00:15:25.653 --> 00:15:27.492
Also, I'd love to know what
did you think of this video?

00:15:27.492 --> 00:15:28.329
Did you like it?

00:15:28.329 --> 00:15:29.851
Which tip was your favorite
from one of the seven?

00:15:29.851 --> 00:15:31.378
Is there an eight, nine, 10 that I missed

00:15:31.378 --> 00:15:32.891
that you want to add to the list?

00:15:32.891 --> 00:15:34.159
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:15:34.159 --> 00:15:36.449
I'm really curious to find
out what you guys have to say.

00:15:36.449 --> 00:15:39.291
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Sahil Baisoya.

00:15:39.291 --> 00:15:41.264
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:15:41.264 --> 00:15:44.551
Your One Word, taking a
picture, and sharing it.

00:15:44.551 --> 00:15:45.772
I really appreciate the support

00:15:45.772 --> 00:15:47.800
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.306
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:49.306 --> 00:15:50.807
I believe in you.

00:15:50.807 --> 00:15:52.418
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:15:52.418 --> 00:15:54.480
and whatever your one word is.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.088
Much love, I'll see you soon.

